    <string name="settings_mediaservers_plex_token_hint">The token of your Plex server. Kept encrypted and never shown again; leave empty to keep the stored one. A new address needs it typed again.</string>
    <string name="settings_mediaservers_api_key_hint">Make one in the server: Dashboard, API keys. Kept encrypted and never shown again; leave empty to keep the stored one. A new address needs it typed again.</string>
    <string name="settings_mediaservers_subsonic_hint">Use an account that may start a library scan. HolyArrs asks for a full scan after new music arrives. The password is kept encrypted; leave empty to keep it.</string>
    <string name="settings_mediaservers_kodi_hint">The user name and password of Kodi\'s web server. HolyArrs asks Kodi to scan each new folder and to clean out removed ones. The password is kept encrypted; leave empty to keep it.</string>
    <string name="settings_mediaservers_plain">Plain password (for LDAP)</string>
    <string name="settings_mediaservers_plain_hint">Sends the password itself, not the safer salted sign-in. Turn on only if the server checks passwords with LDAP. Needs an https or local address.</string>
    <string name="settings_mediaservers_web_url">Address for browsers</string>
    <string name="settings_mediaservers_web_url_hint">Where people open the server on their phone or computer. Adds an Open in button to the title pages it has. Leave empty to use the address above, unless only HolyArrs can reach it (like http://jellyfin:8096).</string>
